# The bytes of each wasm module the web app ships, at most, as it ships: after wasm-opt, before
# compression, by the Nix system that builds it. Each module is `packages.${system}`'s, and an
# aarch64 build of the same revision is not byte for byte an x86_64 one. The size after wasm-opt
# moves with the code by about the bytes the code adds; the brotli size of nearly the same code
# moved by 2.8 KB for 300 bytes added, so build-web.sh prints the brotli bytes, what a first visit
# downloads, and judges nothing by them.
#
# A line is its system's figure for the merged tree, as `nix build` makes it, rounded up to the
# next multiple of 10,000 bytes. scripts/build-web.sh refuses a module over its system's line, or
# one with no line. A line only moves down: app/cli/tests/guards/wasm_budget.rs refuses one raised
# against the merge base by more than 16,000 bytes, unless the pull request says why on a
# `Wasm-growth: <module> +<bytes>: <reason>` line (AGENTS.md, "Releases and `Completes:`").
#
# <module> <system> <bytes>
